title: Upfront treatment of nodal TFH lymphoma
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

* ''Preferred:'' Clinical trial; outcomes with conventional chemotherapy remain suboptimal.
* ''Induction:'' CHOP (cyclophosphamide, doxorubicin, vincristine, prednisone), with etoposide added as CHOEP in selected fit patients; dose-adjusted EPOCH is another option. For CD30-positive disease, brentuximab vedotin–CHP is an option, although TFH-specific benefit is less certain than in systemic anaplastic large-cell lymphoma.
* ''Consolidation:'' Consider autologous stem cell transplantation in eligible patients achieving first complete remission; benefit remains incompletely established. Allogeneic transplantation is not routine in first complete remission.
* ''Less-fit patients:'' Individualize palliative systemic therapy (e.g., romidepsin, belinostat, or gemcitabine) and localized radiotherapy according to symptoms, comorbidities, and goals.

Sources: NCCN T-Cell Lymphomas v2.2026, PTCL-B 1–2, MS-21–24; [[EBMT 2025|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40610175/]].
